git fetch origin - updates branches, commits, tags everything but the local branch
git pull origin - fetch + apply on to your local branch

"A user registers with the newsletter service" is a subscription model wherein they get to read stuff, get updates... nothing else.
So in that case an authentication system is not required for the user but rather the author of the service

Rendered basic html form using rocket templates.. which required importing rocket_dyn_templates crate, attach fairing and then rendering using Template::render

Also learnt that the browser parses html and builds a DOM tree first (which is like identifying all the tags, ids, etc.,)
and then resolving which ids and tags are what.. the browser doesn't process line by line but rather reads the whole html and
then starts processing

created a sqlite db which is an in disk memory db.. next step is to figure out how to get rocket talking to the db